# Lumenora Licensing Notice

This repository contains more than one category of material, and no single license governs every file in the repository. In particular, **Lumenora is not one large MIT-licensed work**: the MIT License in section (A) covers only the project's listed custom shell scripts, and it does not extend to Linux, the NVIDIA drivers, or any Lumenora image or ISO that bundles third-party material.

The licensing rules are:

1. The Lumenora-authored custom shell scripts listed in section (A) are licensed under the MIT License. No other repository material is licensed under the MIT License by this notice.
2. Third-party material, including upstream source code, binaries, firmware, assets, and generated components incorporated into Lumenora, is not relicensed by this repository and remains subject to its own governing license, as stated in section (B). The NVIDIA driver stack is third-party material: it is governed by the NVIDIA Driver License Agreement (section (C)), never by the MIT License.
3. The MIT License (section (A)) does not license, cover, or relicense the NVIDIA driver software, the `lumenora-nvidia` / `lumenora-nvidia-open` images and ISOs as products, or any other third-party component.

For avoidance of doubt:

* Section (A) grants rights only in the files identified there and only to the extent that those files are owned by the Lumenora project and licensed under the MIT License.
* Section (A) does not grant rights in third-party code, third-party assets, firmware, or other upstream material.
* Section (A) does not relicense any build output, image, ISO, container image, RPM, Flatpak, firmware blob, or other artifact produced from the repository.
* Any redistribution of a Lumenora-built artifact must comply with the licenses that apply to every included component.
* MIT licensing of Lumenora's custom shell scripts says nothing about the drivers those scripts interact with; using a script does not create any license in the NVIDIA material it manages.
* Nothing in this notice grants any trademark right, logo right, or brand right in Fedora, KDE, Qt, NVIDIA, or any other third-party mark.

